(text "DDIR IS A FUNCTION OF THE WRITE SIGNAL, INVERTED BY WHETHER THE BUS IS OWNED BY THE CPU BOARD." (rect 1248 1480 2003 1495)(font "Arial" (font_size 8)))
(text "WHEN THE CPU BOARD DOES NOT OWN THE BUS, THE DIRECTION OF THE DATA BUS FOR READS AND WRITES" (rect 1248 1496 2009 1511)(font "Arial" (font_size 8)))
(text "IS REVERSED FOR EXTERNAL MASTERS." (rect 1248 1512 1525 1527)(font "Arial" (font_size 8)))
(text "OTHERWISE, FOR READS, DBEN IS ASSERTED ONLY IN THE FOLLOWING CASES:" (rect 1248 1568 1796 1583)(font "Arial" (font_size 8)))
(text "DEVICE HAS ASSERTED DTACK TO END THE BUS CYCLE" (rect 1264 1624 1649 1639)(font "Arial" (font_size 8)))
(text "2. THE CPU BOARD DOES NOT OWN THE BUS, A READ IS BEING PERFORMED FROM AN ON-BOARD DEVICE, THE" (rect 1248 1640 2009 1655)(font "Arial" (font_size 8)))
(text "DEVICE HAS ASSERTED DTACK TO END THE BUS CYCLE" (rect 1264 1656 1649 1671)(font "Arial" (font_size 8)))
(text "DBEN IS ALWAYS ASSERTED FOR WRITES SO THAT ALL PARTS OF THE SYSTEM SEE THE DATA TO BE WRITTEN." (rect 1248 1552 2005 1567)(font "Arial" (font_size 8)))
(text "1. THE CPU BOARD OWNS THE BUS, A READ IS BEING PERFORMED FROM AN OFF-BOARD DEVICE, THE EXTERNAL" (rect 1248 1608 2024 1623)(font "Arial" (font_size 8)))
